<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duke Wen of Teng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duke Wen of Teng was ruler of the small State of Teng in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a> in the late 4th century BCE. He sought the advice of the philosopher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mencius">Mencius</a> on mourning rites and good government, and Mencius urged him to restore the well-field system of land allotment. Their conversations form a chapter of the book Mencius.</p></div>
